*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.db
# Compose reads the root .env, which holds JWT_SECRET and the database
# password. .env.example is the committed template.
.env
!.env.example
backend/.env
web/.env
mobile/.env
node_modules/
dist/
.expo/

# Object storage when running without a bucket: LocalStorage writes uploaded
# documents here. Test and demo artefacts, never source.
backend/var/

# The demo and test credentials, written out in one place for whoever is
# running this locally. Never committed: a credential file in a public repo is
# a credential file in a search index. `backend/seed.py` remains the source of
# truth, and PASSWORDS.md explains how to override it.
PASSWORDS.md
